# File links in chat

When you mention a file you are working on, just edited, or that the user asked about, make the **file name** a clickable link that opens it in the sidebar editor. Do not leave a bare path the user has to hunt for.

## Format (Cursor chat)

Write the basename as link text, with a workspace-relative path (forward slashes):

[`RULES.md`](RULES.md)

[`SKILL.md`](skills/write-skill/SKILL.md)

Cursor also auto-linkifies backtick-wrapped workspace-relative paths:

`skills/write-skill/SKILL.md`

## Line ranges

Use a Cursor code citation fence (`startLine:endLine:filepath`), not a markdown URL with `#L`.

## Do not

- Use `file://` or `openmd://` in chat (unreliable)
- Use Windows backslashes (`\`) in chat links (they percent-encode and fail to open)
- Use drive-letter markdown links like `[x](C:/...)` (treated as a URI scheme)
- Link every incidental mention of a well-known filename (`package.json` as a concept). Only files in this conversation's work
